1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:10,160
Open source has a new problem. Contributors' AI agents can write ten pull requests in a weekend — and you are still one human reading diffs.

2
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:19,339
Chock is governance as code. Write a policy once, commit it — and your rules travel with every fork.

3
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:32,579
The compiler turns it into the strongest control every agent supports. Git hooks. CI gates. Native hooks in Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot, and VS Code. Across fourteen agents.

4
00:00:34,799 --> 00:00:42,250
So when a contributor's agent stages a credential — on their machine — it is blocked before the pull request exists.

5
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:48,250
What reaches you has already passed your gates — and your CI gate backs it up.

6
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:56,780
Every policy carries an eval suite, and a coverage report that tells you exactly where a guarantee holds — and where it doesn't.

7
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:06,420
A growing catalog of ready policies, including coverage of the full OWASP agentic security top ten — with its limits stated honestly.

8
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,680
Chock. Govern the agent. Review the policy once — not every pull request.
